# AgencyOS — PRODUCTION environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` on the deployment host (or paste into your platform's
# environment-variable UI) and fill in REAL values. Never commit the
# filled-in file — `.env` is gitignored on purpose.
#
# Startup validation: the app refuses to boot if DATABASE_URL is missing
# or is not a `file:` URL (see src/lib/db.ts) — it never silently falls
# back to an empty development database.

# ── REQUIRED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SQLite on the persistent volume. The production container mounts its data
# volume at /app/db (see Dockerfile VOLUME instruction), so the file lives on
# durable infrastructure and survives restarts and redeploys.
DATABASE_URL="file:/app/db/custom.db"

# ── DEMO ACCOUNTS (must stay disabled in production) ───────────────────────
# When true, the login page displays demo credentials via TEST_ACCOUNTS_JSON.
# In production this MUST be "false" and TEST_ACCOUNTS_JSON must be unset,
# so no credentials are ever shown publicly.
ENABLE_TEST_ACCOUNTS="false"
# TEST_ACCOUNTS_JSON — DO NOT SET in production.
